35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found that chasing money for individual sessions takes six hours a month! Also, mid-year joiners need a lot of manual calculations.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Most of our costs are fixed, like hall hire and insurance. Also, many members struggle to pay the full renewal fee at once.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"Past tiered systems caused friction and discouraged lower grades. Additionally, some potential members refuse to commit to a full year upfront.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,Turnout dropped after we added door charges to outings. Some quieter members also feel uneasy about the cost per visit.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's worse than I thought. A quarter of us do two-thirds of the attending, and the same nine people do all the setup.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, if people struggle with one big payment, maybe smaller ones are better? But I'm worried about the treasurer's workload.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, smaller payments mean more chasing. If seventy percent of our costs are fixed, we can't rely on per-event fees to cover the basics.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@May, it seems any ""pay-as-you-go"" approach might actually discourage the people we want to keep.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, that's true, but the ""whole year"" commitment is also scaring people away. We need a middle ground.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,We have a core group doing all the work and paying for people who barely show up. A flat fee feels unfair to the regulars.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,I just don't want the next treasurer to quit. Six hours a month just chasing money sounds exhausting.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,We must ensure the fixed costs are covered. Guesswork won't work. We need a system that guarantees the budget.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We should avoid anything that creates ""grades"" or visible tiers of membership. It kills the inclusive spirit.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"If people feel they are ""paying for nothing"" when they don't attend, they stop coming. We need to remove that guilt.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, if we stick to a flat fee, we're just subsidizing the ghosts of the club. That's not rational.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
