60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option A is easiest for the treasurer, but Option B seems fairer for those who don't come often. Option C is too complex.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option A is the only way to guarantee our fixed costs are covered without constant chasing. B is a financial risk.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,Option C creates the friction I saw in the records. Option B might be too visible. I lean toward Option A.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"Option A makes people feel locked in, which is scary. Option B makes every visit a decision. I prefer Option B.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is a subsidy for the lazy. Option B reflects actual usage. Option C is just a formal version of the same problem.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, but Option B means the treasurer has to chase money every single event! That's the six hours a month I'm worried about.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, if we go with B, and turnout drops, we can't pay the insurance. We'll be bankrupt. A is the only stable choice.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, you're right about the workload. A single annual fee is the most discreet and least burdensome for everyone.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, but if the fee is too high, the taster guests won't join. Option B lowers the barrier to entry.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, the treasurer's time is a cost, but the social resentment of the regulars is a bigger risk. I vote B.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,I can't support B if it makes the job impossible. I'll vote for A to keep things simple and peaceful.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,Stability and predictability are paramount. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,"To protect the club's inclusive nature and the treasurer's sanity, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"I still think B is more inviting, but if it risks the club's existence, I'm torn. I'll stick with B for the members.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I'm staying with B. Fairness in contribution is the only way to stop the complaining.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
